You are building AlgoDesk — a no-code algorithmic trading bot 
constructor for crypto traders.

## Project Overview
Web platform where users can create, backtest, and run trading 
bots on Bybit without writing code. Visual drag-and-drop strategy 
builder with real-time execution.

## Tech Stack
- Backend: Python 3.11 + FastAPI + WebSockets
- Database: PostgreSQL (main) + Redis (cache, live prices)
- Exchange: CCXT library (Bybit as primary)
- Frontend: React 18 + TailwindCSS + Zustand (state)
- Infrastructure: Docker + Docker Compose
- Payments: CryptoBot API (Telegram, USDT)
- Auth: Telegram OAuth (telegram-login-widget)

## Project Structure
/backend
  /api         → FastAPI routes
  /core        → trading engine, bot runner
  /models      → DB models (SQLAlchemy)
  /services    → bybit, backtest, user services
  /workers     → background tasks (bot execution)
/frontend
  /components  → UI components
  /pages       → main pages
  /store       → Zustand state
  /hooks       → custom hooks
/infra
  docker-compose.yml
  .env.example

## Core Features to Build (MVP)
1. Auth — Telegram OAuth login, JWT sessions
2. Exchange connection — user adds Bybit API key/secret, 
   stored encrypted (Fernet)
3. Strategy builder — visual editor with blocks:
   - Entry condition (price crosses MA, RSI threshold, etc.)
   - Exit condition
   - Stop-loss (% or fixed)
   - Take-profit (% or fixed)
   - Position size (% of balance)
4. Paper trading — run strategy with fake balance, 
   real market prices via WebSocket
5. Backtest — run strategy on historical OHLCV data from Bybit, 
   return: total return %, max drawdown, win rate, equity curve
6. Live trading — real execution via Bybit API with position limits
7. Trade log — all orders with timestamp, price, PnL
8. Telegram alerts — notify user when bot opens/closes position 
   or crashes

## Database Models
- User (id, telegram_id, username, api_key_encrypted, created_at)
- Strategy (id, user_id, name, config_json, status, created_at)
- Trade (id, strategy_id, symbol, side, price, amount, pnl, 
  timestamp)
- Subscription (id, user_id, plan, expires_at, paid_in_usdt)

## Key Rules
- Never store API keys in plaintext — always encrypt with Fernet
- All bot instances run as async background tasks via asyncio
- Use CCXT unified interface so adding new exchanges later is easy
- Frontend communicates with backend only via REST + WebSocket
- One active bot per strategy max
- Paper trading and live trading share same engine, 
  different execution layer

